 Collaboration</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cochrane.org">http://www.cochrane.org</ext-link></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><mixed-citation publication-type="other"><article-title>Evidence Based Medicine</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://ebm.bmjjournals.com">http://ebm.bmjjournals.com</ext-link></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><mixed-citation publication-type="other"><article-title>Clinical Evidence</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.clinicalevidence.com">http://www.clinicalevidence.com</ext-link></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><mixed-citation publication-type="other"><article-title>The ACP Journal Club</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.acpjc.org">http://www.acpjc.org</ext-link></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Sim</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Owens</surname><given-names>DK</given-names></name><name><surname>Lavori</surname><given-names>PW</given-names></name><name><surname>Rennels</surname><given-names>GD</given-names></name><article-title>Electronic Trial Banks: A Complementary Method for Reporting Randomized Trials</article-title><source>Medical Decision Making</source><year>2000</year><volume>20</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>440</fpage><lpage>450</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1177/0272989X0002000408</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11059477</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><mixed-citation publication-type="other"><name><surname>P</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>I</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>J</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Aronson</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><article-title>Argumentative feedback: a linguistically-motivated term expansion for information retrieval</article-title><source>Proceedings of the ACL, Association for Computational Linguistics</source><year>2006</year><fpage>675</fpage><lpage>682</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Moher</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Schultz</surname><given-names>KF</given-names></name><name><surname>Altman</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><article-title>The CONSORT Statment: revised recommendations for improving the quality of reports of parallel-group randomized trials</article-title><source>Journal of the American Medical Association</source><year>2001</year><volume>285</volume><fpage>1987</fpage><lpage>1991</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/jama.285.15.1987</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11308435</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><mixed-citation publication-type="other"><article-title>The Journal of the American Medical Association</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://jama.ama-assn.org/">http://jama.ama-assn.org/</ext-link></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B16"><mixed-citation publication-type="other"><article-title>Annals of Internal Medicine</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.annals.org/">http://www.annals.org/</ext-link></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B17"><mixed-citation publication-type="other"><article-title>Heart</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://heart.bmj.com/">http://heart.bmj.com/</ext-link></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B18"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Mann</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><source>Rhetorical Structure Theory: A Theory of Text Organization, Volume ISI/RS-87-190</source><year>1987</year><publisher-name>Los Angeles, CA: ISI: Information Sciences Institute</publisher-name></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B19"><mixed-citation publication-type="other"><name><surname>Sporleder</surname